
                             SYSTEM VARIABLES
                             ================

There are a number of built in system variables that are read only. They
are the following:

argv$(argc)  - Command line arguments following "--"
version$     - Interpreter version
build_date$  - Build date of the binary
current_dir$ - Current working directory
username$    - Unix user name
usergroup$   - Group of user

argc       - Number of command line arguments following "--"
last_error - Number of the last error (can be used with error$())
num_errors - Total number of errors 
num_pens   - Total number of pens (text colours)
num_papers - Total number of papers (background colours)
num_styles - Total number of text styles

screen_width  - Width of the screen/terminal. If the width cannot be determined
                (eg with serial terminals) then it is set to 0.
screen_height - Height of the screen/terminal. Also set to 0 if cannot be
                determined.

pi              - Value of PI.
degs_per_radian - Number of degrees in a radian.
